    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0906" n="896" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg896"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Pacific War/6–2746</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the State Department Member of the
                        State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hilldring</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">SWN–4471</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-06-27">27 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>By informal action on 25 June 1946 the State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee
                    approved SWNCC 258/5 as amended by SWNCC 258/6 and SWNCC 258/7.</p>
                <p>A copy of the revised approved paper is forwarded herewith. It is requested that
                    the Department of State transmit the draft note in Appendix “C”<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d618-f1"/> of the revised approved paper to the Chinese
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>For the State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee: <lb/>
                    <signed>J. H. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hilldring</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d618-a1.xml" xpointer="d618-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d618-f1" n="25" xml:id="d618-f1-content">
                <p>Draft note not printed; for text, see telegram No. 397, July 2, 6 p.m., to the
                    Embassy in China, <ref target="#pg905">p. 905</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
